{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Swift_Strike","to":"Swift Strike"},{"from":"Defend_(Silent)","to":"Defend (Silent)"},{"from":"Quick_Slash","to":"Quick Slash"},{"from":"Strike_(Ironclad)","to":"Strike (Ironclad)"},{"from":"Defend_(Ironclad)","to":"Defend (Ironclad)"},{"from":"Infinite_Blades","to":"Infinite Blades"},{"from":"Blade_Dance","to":"Blade Dance"},{"from":"Static_Discharge","to":"Static Discharge"},{"from":"Meteor_Strike","to":"Meteor Strike"},{"from":"Infernal_Blade","to":"Infernal Blade"}],"pages":{"1809":{"pageid":1809,"ns":0,"title":"Adrenaline","revisions":[{"revid":56304,"parentid":56193,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Adrenaline\n| Image       = Green-Adrenaline.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Gain ({{Icon|GE}};{{Icon|GE}} {{Icon|GE}}).<br>Draw 2 cards.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw, Energy, Exhaust\n}}\n{{C|Adrenaline}} is a 0 {{Icon|GE}}-cost, {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws 2 cards, generates 1 (2) {{Icon|GE}}, and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\nAdrenaline provides card draw and {{Icon|GE}} generation with no up front cost, and as such, can benefit nearly any deck to some degree. However, there are some cases where it is particularly useful:\n* Cards which benefit from having many '''cards in hand''', such as {{C|Calculated Gamble}} and {{C|Storm of Steel}}.\n* '''High cost cards''' which are important to play consistently, such as {{C|Nightmare}} and {{C|Wraith Form}}.\n* '''X-cost cards''' such as {{C|Malaise}} or {{C|Skewer}}\n* Having more Energy also benefit's Silent's other draw options, as you can pay for cards such as {{C|Acrobatics}} and {{C|Backflip}} while still having Energy for the cards they draw.\n* Decks that want to play '''many cards in one turn''', such as those making use of {{R|Shuriken}}, {{R|Kunai}}, {{R|Ornamental Fan}}, {{R|Nunchaku}}, or {{C|Panache}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\nGiven how many strategies can benefit from Adrenaline, it is actually easier to list things which ''don't'':\n* '''{{R|Snecko Eye}}''' often makes Adrenaline cost more than 0, reducing the {{Icon|GE}} it generates, and often even making it cost Energy.\n* '''{{R|Velvet Choker}}''' caps your turn at 6 card plays, preventing the sorts of big turns Adrenaline enables.\n* Similarly, '''{{C|Normality}}''' can cause issues with attempting big turns. This can be mitigated with ways to discard or exhaust the Normality, as well as by not playing Adrenaline as your third card for the turn.\n* Certain fights, most notably [[Gremlin Nob]], [[Chosen]], [[Time Eater]], and the [[Corrupt Heart]], have '''downsides to playing cards''' which may make it worthwhile not to play Adrenaline.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2059":{"pageid":2059,"ns":0,"title":"Barrage","revisions":[{"revid":56893,"parentid":55636,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Barrage\n|Image       = Blue-Barrage.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (4;6) damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb.\n|InteractsWith = Channel\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Channel}}\n{{C|Barrage}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Cracked Core}}, {{R|Symbiotic Virus}} and {{R|Nuclear Battery}} each give Barrage 1 additional hit directly from the start of combat. {{C|Chill|Chill+}} gives ''at least'' one extra hit always in your starting hand.\n\n* {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, and {{P|Potion of Capacity}} give additional [[Orbs#Orb Slots|Orb Slots]], allowing Barrage to hit more times total.\n\n* Benefits once from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}} per hit, so for every {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Reducing the amount of Orb Slots through {{C|Consume}} reduces the potential of {{C|Barrage}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The {{M|Shelled Parasite}} is shown in this card's artwork as well as its [[Beta Art]].\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1797":{"pageid":1797,"ns":0,"title":"Blade Dance","revisions":[{"revid":56363,"parentid":55651,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Blade Dance\n| Image       = Green-BladeDance.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Add (3;4) {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} into your hand.\n}} \n{{Small Card Infobox|Shiv}}\n{{C|Blade Dance}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It adds 3 (4 if upgraded) {{C|Shiv}} cards to your hand. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies === \n* The damage of each {{C|Shiv}} will be increased by the amount of {{BD|Accuracy}} you have, which can be obtained from {{C|Accuracy}}.\n\n* {{R|Wrist Blade}} increases the damage of every {{C|Shiv}} by 4.\n\n* Anything that benefits from {{KW|Exhaust}} will be triggered by playing {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}.\n\n* As {{C|Blade Dance}} gives many {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards, it synergizes with:\n** {{R|Shuriken}}, {{R|Kunai}}, and {{R|Ornamental Fan}}, which can be triggered consistently.\n** {{C|Envenom}}.\n** {{C|Finisher}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If a {{C|Shiv}} generated by this card exceeds your hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n\n* As playing {{C|Blade Dance}} and all {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} created by it results in a lot of cards being played, {{C|Blade Dance}} has many interactions with things that count cards being played:\n** Effects such as {{BD|After Image}}, {{BD|Thousand Cuts}} and {{BD|Beat of Death}} will be triggered often.\n** Counters of things like {{C|Panache}} and {{R|Ink Bottle}} will be increased.\n*** An upgraded {{C|Blade Dance}} can trigger {{BD|Panache}} by itself.\n** Card limits such as from {{R|Velvet Choker}} or {{BD|Time Warp}} will be reached more easily.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Blade Dance card buffed. 2 -> 3 shivs.\n** Blade Dance+ card buffed. 3 -> 4 shivs.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 36: Power Through'''\n** Blade Dance card rarity lowered from Uncommon -> Common\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1486":{"pageid":1486,"ns":0,"title":"Defend (Ironclad)","revisions":[{"revid":56341,"parentid":50388,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Defend (Ironclad)\n| DisplayName = Defend\n| Image       = Red-Defend.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Basic\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain (5;8) {{KW|Block}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Defend (Ironclad)|Defend}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 5 (8 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}.\n\nThis page is for the Ironclad's version of Defend, go here for {{C|Defend (Silent)}}, {{C|Defend (Defect)}}, {{C|Defend (Watcher)}}\n\n== Obtaining Defend ==\nThe [[Ironclad]] starts with 4 copies of {{C|Defend (Ironclad)|Defend}} in his deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Falling Event can now hit Strikes and Defends, making the event potentially not as bad.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1488":{"pageid":1488,"ns":0,"title":"Defend (Silent)","revisions":[{"revid":56343,"parentid":50468,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Defend (Silent)\n| DisplayName = Defend\n| Image       = Green-Defend.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Basic\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain (5;8) {{KW|Block}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Defend (Silent)|Defend}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 5 (8 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}.\n\nThis page is for the Silent's version of Defend, go here for {{C|Defend (Ironclad)}}, {{C|Defend (Defect)}}, {{C|Defend (Watcher)}}\n\n== Obtaining Defend ==\nThe [[Silent]] starts with 5 copies of {{C|Defend (Silent)|Defend}} in her deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Silent's starting Strikes are put before Defends (to be consistent with other characters)\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Falling Event can now hit Strikes and Defends, making the event potentially not as bad.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1457":{"pageid":1457,"ns":0,"title":"Eruption","revisions":[{"revid":56338,"parentid":55762,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Eruption\n| Image       = Purple-Eruption.png\n| Color       = Purple\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Basic\n| Cost        = 2\n| CostPlus    = 1\n| Description = Deal 9 damage. Enter {{KW|Wrath}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Wrath\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Wrath}}\n{{C|Eruption}} is a 2 (1 if upgraded) {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 9 damage and makes you enter the {{KW|Wrath}} {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n== Obtaining Eruption ==\nThe [[Watcher]] starts the game with one copy of {{C|Eruption}} in her deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards, but can be obtained in the {{E|Match and Keep}} Event. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{C|Eruption}} first deals damage and only then makes you enter {{KW|Wrath}}, meaning its own damage is not yet doubled if you were not already in {{KW|Wrath}}. \n\n=== Synergies ===\n* When entering {{KW|Wrath}} if you are not in {{KW|Wrath}} yet:\n** If you have {{BD|Rushdown}} from {{C|Rushdown}}, you will draw that many cards.\n** You will switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n*** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n*** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n*** If you were in the {{KW|Calm}} {{KW|Stance}} before, you will gain 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''', or 3 if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n* Being in {{KW|Wrath}} changes the effects of some cards:\n** {{C|Halt}} will give its additional {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{C|Indignation}} will apply {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* While in {{KW|Wrath}}, all {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} damage you deal is doubled, but you also take double damage from enemy attacks.{{KW|Wrath}} only doubles damage from {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, not from effects such as {{BD|Panache}} or {{BD|Thorns}}, or relics such as {{R|Mercury Hourglass}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{KW|Wrath}} is worse than the {{KW|Divinity}} {{KW|Stance}} in every way except for the aformentioned ones, using {{C|Eruption}} while in {{KW|Divinity}} is generally bad, if it does not end combat.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1867":{"pageid":1867,"ns":0,"title":"Headbutt","revisions":[{"revid":50397,"parentid":35930,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Headbutt\n|Image       = Red-Headbutt.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (9;12) damage.<br>Put a card from your discard pile on top of your draw pile.\n}}\n{{C|Headbutt}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 9 (12 if upgraded) damage, and allows you to select one card in your discard pile to place on top of your draw pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Although {{C|Mayhem}} plays the top card of the draw pile, it cannot be used in tandem with {{C|Headbutt}} to play a specific card, as {{C|Mayhem}} activates ''after'' cards are drawn at the start of your turn, meaning the card will already be in hand.\n** This could still be achieved if you used {{C|Headbutt}} on more cards than you draw at the start of your turn. \n\n=== Other ===\n* If there is only one card in your discard pile, it will automatically be placed on top of your draw pile.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Discard/Draw panels can be viewed during screens such as Survivor, Headbutt, and Gambling Chip now.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!'''\n** Cards now teleport instantly (logically, not visually) fixing race conditions with Headbutt and Unceasing Top.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1927":{"pageid":1927,"ns":0,"title":"Infernal Blade","revisions":[{"revid":56754,"parentid":50432,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Infernal Blade\n| Image       = Red-InfernalBlade.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| CostPlus    = 0\n| Description = Add a random Attack into your hand.<br>It costs 0 this turn.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Infernal Blade}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|RE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It will generate a random {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card, which will have its normal cost replaced by 0 for this turn. {{C|Infernal Blade}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself. X-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards generated this way will still consume all your energy. \n\n{{C|Infernal Blade}} can only generate cards you can find in card rewards through character choice or custom run modifiers, and is not affected by {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* Some {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards cannot be generated, as they have some permanent effect out of combat, or can only be obtained from another source.\n** {{C|Feed}}\n** {{C|Reaper}}\n** {{C|Lesson Learned}}\n** {{C|Bite}}\n** {{C|Ritual Dagger}}\n** {{C|Shiv}}\n** {{C|Smite}}\n** {{C|Through Violence}}\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like  Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2055":{"pageid":2055,"ns":0,"title":"Infinite Blades","revisions":[{"revid":55823,"parentid":50514,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Infinite Blades\n|Image       = Green-InfiniteBlades.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = (;{{KW|Innate}}. )At the start of your turn, add a {{C|Shiv}} into your hand.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Infinite Blades}} {{Small Card Infobox|Shiv}}\n{{C|Infinite Blades}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 {{BD|Infinite Blades}}, which adds 1 {{C|Shiv}} to your hand at the start of every turn. If upgraded, it has {{KW|Innate}}, meaning it will always appear in your first hand of combat.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Infinite Blades}} takes effect ''before'' your cards are drawn. This means that having a high amount of {{BD|Infinite Blades}} can cause you to draw less cards at the start of your turn due to the hand size limit.\n\n=== Synergies === \n* The damage of each {{C|Shiv}} will be increased by the amount of {{BD|Accuracy}} you have, which can be obtained from {{C|Accuracy}}.\n\n* {{R|Wrist Blade}} increases the damage of every {{C|Shiv}} by 4.\n* Anything that benefits from {{KW|Exhaust}} will be triggered by {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}.\n\n* Anything that benefits from {{KW|Exhaust}} will be triggered by playing {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If a {{C|Shiv}} generated by this card exceeds your hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for Infinite Blades power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Draw 1 Shiv -> Add 1 Shiv into your hand. Infinite Blades Power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Effects that spawn cards in your hand at start of turn like Infinite Blades and Ninja Scroll will now trigger before card draw.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2469":{"pageid":2469,"ns":0,"title":"Madness","revisions":[{"revid":55847,"parentid":50731,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Madness\n|Image       = Colorless-Madness.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = Reduce the cost of a random card in your hand to 0 this combat.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Madness}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It reduces the cost of one random card in hand to 0 for the rest of combat. \n\nIt will not target X-cost cards or cards that already permanently cost 0 {{Icon|CE}} '''Energy''', but will target cards that have their cost temporarily reduced to 0, through for example {{C|Setup}}, {{R|Mummified Hand}} or {{P|Liquid Memories}}.\n\n== Obtaining Madness ==\n{{C|Madness}} is a card that can be obtained regularly, but can also be obtained through the {{E|Winding Halls}} event by choosing {{Frame|Embrace Madness}}.\n\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* The randomization of {{BD|Confused}} or {{P|Snecko Oil}} will override the cost reduction of the card targeted by {{C|Madness}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** All-Out Attack, Madness, and Reboot cards no longer affect Card Rewards when used (rng issue).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Madness is nerfed (costs 1 now). Upgrade cost 1 -> 0.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Bullet Time now affects all cards currently in hand, works with Madness, and no longer applies a Power to you.\n\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** When you use Madness, the card affected flashes gold now.\n** Fix for Bite cards not loading correctly (it gave you Madness cards) when resuming a run.\n** If a card fails to be identified you now get a Madness instead of crashing.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2101":{"pageid":2101,"ns":0,"title":"Meteor Strike","revisions":[{"revid":55861,"parentid":50624,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Meteor Strike\n|Image       = Blue-MeteorStrike.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 5\n|Description = Deal (24;30) damage. <br>{{KW|Channel}} 3 {{KW|Plasma}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Plasma}}\n{{C|Meteor Strike}} is a 5 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}}. <!---It deals 24 (30) damage, and {{KW|Channel|Channels}} 3 {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}}.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Meteor Strike can be difficult to play for the first time due to its substantial cost. Luckily, [[Defect]] has various ways to produce a lot of {{Icon|BE}} Energy:\n** {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}}\n** {{C|TURBO}}\n** {{C|Recycle}}\n** {{C|Double Energy}}\n** {{C|Aggregate}}\n** {{C|Fission}}\n* In addition, as {{R|Snecko Eye}} can only make cards cost up to 3, it will ''always'' reduce the cost of Meteor Strike.\n* Once Meteor Strike has been played once, the {{Icon|BE}} from the {{KW|Plasma}} Orbs it generates makes playing it again much easier.\n\n* {{C|Meteor Strike}} gets a damage increase from {{R|Strike Dummy}} and adds to the damage of {{C|Perfected Strike}}.\n\n* Meteor Strike is a particularly good target for {{R|Necronomicon}} and {{C|Echo Form}}. Assuming you have 3 Orb Slots, the second copy will {{KW|Evoke}} the Orbs generated by the first copy, immediately repaying 6 {{Icon|BE}} while doing substantial damage.\n\n* Due to its high cost, Meteor Strike is a good target for {{C|Recycle}}, if you don't need to play it in a given combat.\n\n* The {{Icon|BE}} Energy generated by Meteor Strike's {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}} allows for playing other expensive and X cost cards, such as {{C|Echo Form}}, {{C|Tempest}}, {{C|Reinforced Body}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}}.\n\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Other Orb sources, such as {{C|Darkness}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, can be very helpful for {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}} more frequently.\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{BD|Focus}} has no effect on {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}}, {{C|Consume}} removing an Orb Slot is a strict downside for {{KW|Plasma}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Not counting X-cost cards or {{C|Masterful Stab}}, both of which can be played for arbitrarily large amounts of Energy, Meteor Strike is the most expensive card in the game.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** Fixed issue where Strike (blue), Thunder Strike, and Meteor Strike weren't used by Perfected Strike.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2020":{"pageid":2020,"ns":0,"title":"Outmaneuver","revisions":[{"revid":55882,"parentid":53368,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Outmaneuver\n|Image       = Green-Outmaneuver.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Next turn,<br>gain {{Icon|GE}} {{Icon|GE}}(; {{Icon|GE}}).\n|Keywords    = Energy\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Energized (Silent)}}\n{{C|Outmaneuver}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Energized (Silent)}}, which gives you that amount of extra {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' at the start of your next turn.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1956":{"pageid":1956,"ns":0,"title":"Pain","revisions":[{"revid":56780,"parentid":55883,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Pain\n|Image       = Curse-Pain.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Curse\n|Cost        = -2\n|NoUpgrade   = true\n|Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>While in hand, lose 1 HP when other cards are played.\n|GivesToPlayer = Lose HP, Unplayable\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}}\n{{C|Pain}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card. While it is in your hand, you will lose 1 HP every time you play a card.\n\n== Obtaining Pain ==\nLike most {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}}, Pain can be obtained from anything that gives a random Curse:\n* Can be part of Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a reward.\n* {{E|Match and Keep}}.\n* {{R|Cursed Key}}.\n* {{KW|Transform|Transforming}} another Curse.\n\nIn addition, Pain can be obtained from the {{E|Ominous Forge}} Event when choosing {{Frame|Rummage}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n<!--- The other three's order doesn't really matter, but for posterity I found pain > thorns > scales > beat --->\n* Pain will hurt you ''before'' any of {{BD|Thorns}}, {{BD|Sharp Hide}}, or {{BD|Beat of Death}}.\n* Pain will hurt you ''before'' the card is resolves, and therefore before any self inflicted HP loss the card may cause.\n** Because of this, playing {{C|Rupture}} with Pain in hand will not immediately gain you a {{BD|Strength}}, as the HP loss occurs before the {{BD|Rupture}} [[Buffs|Buff]] is in effect.\n** However, {{C|Blood for Blood}} is still played for the price listed on it, as the cost is paid by the time you lose HP.\n* If a card is double played, you will lose HP from Pain for both card plays. Moreover, you will not lose HP from the second card until after the first card is played.\n* {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} Pain with {{R|Blue Candle}} will only hurt you due to Blue Candle, ''not'' due to Pain as well.\n\n=== Synergies ===\nAs Pain is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you 1 {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for 1 HP. \n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you 6 max HP if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' Omamori.\n\nThe HP loss from Pain can be:\n* Negated with {{BD|Buffer}}, via {{R|Fossilized Helix}} and {{C|Buffer}}.\n* Reduced by 1 with {{R|Tungsten Rod}}.\n\nThe HP loss from Pain can also be used to your benefit: \n* Losing HP causes {{R|Runic Cube}} to draw you a card.\n* {{C|Blood for Blood}} will have its cost reduced for the rest of combat.\n* The HP loss is counted as being from a card, so {{C|Rupture}} will gain you {{BD|Strength}}. Due to this, it is sometimes desirable to keep Pain around as the [[Ironclad]], as this combo can be used to scale very rapidly.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If you have multiple copies of {{C|Pain}} in your hand, each one causes separate life loss. Therefore, they can all be completely negated by {{R|Tungsten Rod}}, trigger {{C|Rupture}} and {{R|Runic Cube}} independently, and discount {{C|Blood for Blood}} multiple times, but will each separately consume a stack of {{BD|Buffer}} and make {{C|Masterful Stab}} more expensive.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as Pain, it cannot be played.\n* The HP loss from Pain causes {{C|Masterful Stab}} to have its cost increased for the rest of combat.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2476":{"pageid":2476,"ns":0,"title":"Purity","revisions":[{"revid":50736,"parentid":36936,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Purity\n|Image       = Colorless-Purity.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = {{KW|Exhaust}} up to (3;5) cards in your hand.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Purity}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It allows you to select up to 3 (5 if upgraded) cards in your hand to {{KW|Exhaust}}, after which it {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} itself.\n\n== Obtaining Purity ==\n{{C|Purity}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Purity card wording improvements.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Purity card rework. 2 cards -> 'up to' 3 cards -> 5 cards on upgrade.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2022":{"pageid":2022,"ns":0,"title":"Quick Slash","revisions":[{"revid":50489,"parentid":36298,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Quick Slash\n|Image       = Green-QuickSlash.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (8;12) damage.<br>Draw 1 card.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Quick Slash}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n\n=== Synergies ===\n\n=== Neutral ===\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n\n== Trivia ==\n\n== Update History ==\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:ToUpdate]]\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2040":{"pageid":2040,"ns":0,"title":"Setup","revisions":[{"revid":50521,"parentid":36330,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Setup\n|Image       = Green-Setup.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = Put a card from your hand on top of your draw pile.<br>It costs 0 until played.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{C|Setup}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* An {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card set to 0 {{Icon|GE}}  Energy by this card will get a damage increase from {{R|Wrist Blade}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The discount originating from this card will also be copied when the affected card is copied by {{C|Nightmare}} or {{C|Dual Wield}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1'''\n** Fixed Normality card not stopping cards affected by Setup and Forethought.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Fix for Mummified Hand relic targeting cards with costs lowered by Setup or Forethought.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Card copy effects like Dual Wield should now also copy the \"free to play once\" effect from cards like Setup and Forethought.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n** Wrist Blade relic now works with cards that are cost 0 via Setup or Forethought.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2095":{"pageid":2095,"ns":0,"title":"Static Discharge","revisions":[{"revid":55956,"parentid":50607,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Static Discharge\n|Image       = Blue-StaticDischarge.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Whenever you receive unblocked attack damage, {{KW|Channel}} (1;2) {{KW|Lightning}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Static Discharge}}{{C|Static Discharge}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}}. <!---Once played, it will {{KW|Channel}} 1 (2) {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} whenever you receive {{KW|Block|unblocked}} attack damage from an enemy.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Static Discharge will {{KW|Channel}} the Orb ''immediately'' upon receiving the damage, before the enemy turn can continue. This can {{KW|Evoke}} Orbs in the middle of an attack:\n** If a {{KW|Lightning}} or {{KW|Dark}} Orb is Evoked, the damage can kill an enemy. If it is the enemy currently attacking, it will die immediately, ending the attack even if there were additional hits remaining. \n*** If an enemy dies this way while you have {{R|Gremlin Horn}} (and the combat does not end), you will receive {{Icon|BE}} and draw cards after the current attack has concluded. The cards will be kept until your next turn, while the {{Icon|BE}} will be lost unless you have {{R|Ice Cream}}.\n** If a {{KW|Frost}} Orb is Evoked, the {{KW|Block}} will be applied immediately. This will reduce subsequent damage, even if those are further hits of the same attack. \n** If a {{KW|Plasma}} Orb is Evoked, the {{Icon|BE}} it generates will be lost, unless you have {{R|Ice Cream}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Static Discharge is particularly effective in fights with multi-hit attacks, especially including [[Hexaghost]], [[Byrd|Byrds]], [[Book of Stabbing]], and the [[Corrupt Heart]]\n* {{R|Torii}} and {{R|Tungsten Rod}} can both decrease the amount of damage you receive while still allowing Static Discharge to trigger.\n\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Other Orb sources, such as {{C|Darkness}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, can be very helpful for {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} more frequently.\n* {{C|Thunder Strike}} hits more times for each {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat, and {{C|Electrodynamics}} makes {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} hit all enemies.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Static Discharge will only {{KW|Channel}} Orbs when taking attack damage. Other sources of enemy damage such as {{BD|Thorns}} and {{BD|Beat of Death}} will not trigger it.\n* Static Discharge requires you to actually take damage to trigger: if an enemy is doing 0 damage (perhaps due to having negative {{BD|Strength}}), it will not trigger even if you have 0 {{KW|Block}}.\n** Similarly, damage prevented with {{BD|Buffer}} will not trigger Static Discharge.\n** However, as {{R|Tungsten Rod}} reduces ''HP Loss'', rather than damage, it is possible to lose no HP while triggering Static Discharge, if the attack would have done precisely 1 unblocked damage.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making {{KW|Lightning}} Orbs less effective.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\nStatic Discharge card now clarifies that it triggers when you receive unblocked attack damage.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1318":{"pageid":1318,"ns":0,"title":"Strike (Ironclad)","revisions":[{"revid":43163,"parentid":35922,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} {{Card Infobox\n|Name=Strike (Ironclad)\n|DisplayName=Strike\n|Image=Red-Strike.png\n|Color=Red\n|Type=Attack\n|Rarity=Basic\n|Cost=1\n|Description=Deal (6;9) damage.\n}}\n{{C|Strike (Ironclad)|Strike}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 6 (9 if upgraded) damage.\n\nThis page is for Ironclad's version of Strike. Go here for {{C|Strike (Silent)}}, {{C|Strike (Defect)}}, {{C|Strike (Watcher)}}.\n\n== Obtaining Strike ==\nThe [[Ironclad]] starts with 5 copies of {{C|Strike (Ironclad)|Strike}} in his deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Strike (Ironclad)|Strike}} gets a damage increase of 3 from {{R|Strike Dummy}}, and adds to the damage of {{C|Perfected Strike}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Falling Event can now hit Strikes and Defends, making the event potentially not as bad.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2447":{"pageid":2447,"ns":0,"title":"Swift Strike","revisions":[{"revid":50737,"parentid":36937,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Swift Strike\n|Image       = Colorless-SwiftStrike.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Deal (7;10) damage.\n}}\n{{C|Swift Strike}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 7 (10 if upgraded) damage.\n\n== Obtaining Swift Strike ==\n{{C|Swift Strike}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Swift Strike card buffed. Damage increased from 6 -> 7.\n** Swift Strike+ card buffed. Damage increased from 9 -> 10.\n\n* '''Slay the Spire 1.0: Farewell Early Access'''\n** Swift Strike's VFX is now a blunt VFX rather than slice VFX.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Swift Strike card buff: 5 -. 6 damage. Swift Strike+ buff: 8 -> 9 damage.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Swift Strike+. 5 -> 8 damage\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2100":{"pageid":2100,"ns":0,"title":"Tempest","revisions":[{"revid":55972,"parentid":50611,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Tempest\n|Image       = Blue-Tempest.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = -1\n|Description = {{KW|Channel}} (X;X+1) {{KW|Lightning}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}}\n{{C|Tempest}} is an X {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}. It {{KW|Channel|Channels}} X (X+1) {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}}, then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* If an Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} by Tempest causes you to gain {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' due to for example {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} a {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orb}} or killing an enemy with {{R|Gremlin Horn}}, the value of X will not change and that newly generated {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' will not be consumed.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Chemical X}} makes {{C|Tempest}} apply 2 more times, regardless of the amount of {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' used to play it.\n* If played using {{P|Distilled Chaos}}, {{C|Havoc}}, or {{C|Omniscience}}, it will play for the full current {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' without actually using any.\n* Can be used with 0 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' to advance {{R|Ink Bottle}} or {{R|Letter Opener}}.\n* {{C|Tempest}} works best when played with large amounts of {{Icon|BE}}. Luckily, [[Defect]] has various ways to do so:\n** {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}}\n** {{C|TURBO}}\n** {{C|Recycle}}\n** {{C|Double Energy}}\n** {{C|Aggregate}}\n** {{C|Fission}}\n\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Other Orb sources, such as {{C|Darkness}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, can be very helpful for {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} more frequently.\n* {{C|Thunder Strike}} hits more times for each {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat, and {{C|Electrodynamics}} makes {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} hit all enemies.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If {{C|Tempest}} is duplicated with an effect such as a {{P|Duplication Potion}} or {{C|Burst}}, the value of '''X''' will also be used for the copy.\n* Being an X-cost, {{C|Tempest}} can be {{C|Recycle|Recycled}} to double the current {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy'''.\n* It will not count as a 0-cost card for {{C|Scrape}} or {{C|All for One}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making {{KW|Lightning}} Orbs less effective.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Corruption and other cost reducing cards no longer make X cost cards like Transmutation and Malaise display cost 0.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}